Template: partman-scubed3/commit_failed
Type: error
Description: The partition table could not be written
 An error occurred while writing the changes to the disks. scubed3 is not
 configured.

Template: partman-scubed3/no_math64
Type: error
Description: The shell of the installer has no 64 bit arithmetic
 partman-scubed3 needs it to compute the sizes of the blocks. scubed3
 cannot be configured with this installer.

Template: partman-scubed3/no_base
Type: error
Description: No base device for scubed3
 No partition is used as the base device of scubed3. Choose a partition
 (or make one in free space), and set "Use as:" to "base device for
 scubed3". Then choose "Configure scubed3" again.

Template: partman-scubed3/too_many_bases
Type: error
Description: More than one base device for scubed3
 The installed system can use only one base device of scubed3. Use only one
 partition as "base device for scubed3".

Template: partman-scubed3/too_large
Type: error
Description: ${DEVICE} is too large for scubed3
 scubed3 cannot use this partition as its base device. Use a smaller
 partition (at most some tens of terabytes).

Template: partman-scubed3/options
Type: string
Description: Options of the scubed3 daemon:
 The sizes of the blocks are not stored on the base device: the same -m
 (mesoblock size) and -M (macroblock size) must be used forever. The
 default is chosen for the size of the base device. Change this only if you
 know what you are doing, for example to use an existing base device with
 the sizes it was made with.

Template: partman-scubed3/store_type
Type: select
Choices-C: new, existing
Choices: A new scubed3 store (the partition is filled with random data), An existing scubed3 store (keep the data on the partition)
Default: new
Description: What is on ${DEVICE}?
 scubed3 hides encrypted partitions in a device full of random data:
 without its passphrase a partition cannot be told apart from unused space.
 .
 A new store starts with random data on the whole partition. If the
 partition already holds scubed3 partitions, choose the existing store: you
 need its salt (in /etc/scubed3.conf of the system that made it) and the
 passphrases of ALL its partitions.

Template: partman-scubed3/fill
Type: boolean
Default: true
Description: Fill ${DEVICE} with random data?
 All data on ${DEVICE} will be overwritten with random data. This is the
 last opportunity to abort.
 .
 This can take long on a large partition. Without it, the old data on the
 partition shows which blocks scubed3 has written, and which not: do not
 skip it, unless the partition was filled with random data before.

